WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.590
Waimakariri District needs more Civil Defence
volunteers.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:09.020
If you’re 18 years or older, you can join
us and help protect our community.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.340
Our Welfare Team supports those who cannot
look after themselves during emergencies.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.490
We do information, a shoulder to lean on.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.760
We could be issuing them with blankets, sorting
out beds, anybody in the community can join us.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.100
Our Sector Post teams scan their local areas
for people who need help and for dangers to

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.320
the community.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.390
Getting information out to people, what's
the local situation?

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.000
What's things are expected to develop?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.699
It's rewarding to be able to help them through
that situation.

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:42.130
Our Rescue Team engages in a wide range of
emergency tasks and carries out rescues.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:48.340
If you have a hint on interest, then it's
well worth coming down to our open night.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.629
It also has a cadet programme for those aged
15-18 years, which provides hands-on rescue

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:55.820
training and excellent life skills.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.679
Basic first aid, ropes training, how to respond
to floods and storms...

00:01:00.679 --> 00:01:05.089
It's really interesting finding out what we
do, there's so much that we do that people

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:06.089
don't know about.

00:01:06.089 --> 00:01:12.710
Come to our information night on Wednesday
1st March, meet our teams and find your place.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.080
Come along and find out.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:19.369
It's not all physical, it's not all mental,
it's simply being trained up and helping out

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:20.939
when things go wrong.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:26.480
Support your community in emergencies and
volunteer with Civil Defence.

